This service downloads third-party engines and models on demand when
MaiPai Home asks it to (llama.cpp, MLX-based servers, ComfyUI, speech
runtimes, and the models the household selects). None of them are
vendored here. Each is fetched from its pinned upstream URL, checksum
verified, and used under its own licence, which the Stack records with
the download and reports before selection. Attributions for anything this
repo redistributes are listed here as they are added.

- hono (MIT) - https://hono.dev (the backend HTTP framework)
- @hono/zod-openapi (MIT) - https://github.com/honojs/middleware (OpenAPI schemas for the backend routes)
- @scalar/hono-api-reference (MIT) - https://github.com/scalar/scalar (the in-browser API reference for the backend)
- zod (MIT) - https://zod.dev (schema validation for the backend routes)
- drizzle-orm (Apache-2.0) - https://orm.drizzle.team (the backend database layer)
- drizzle-kit (MIT) - https://orm.drizzle.team (generating the backend database schema)
- typescript (Apache-2.0) - https://www.typescriptlang.org/ (the backend language)
- @types/bun (MIT) - https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/master/types/bun (type definitions for the backend)
- @huggingface/gguf (MIT) - https://github.com/huggingface/huggingface.js (GGUF header and remote range parser)
- @huggingface/hub (MIT) - https://github.com/huggingface/huggingface.js (model metadata and file lists for provenance)
